  abstract = {Digital Twins enable central Industry 4.0 use cases, such as changeable production and an efficient lot size one. However, what do they need to look like? Our Industry 4.0 expert Frank Schnicke (www.linkedin.com/in/frank-schnicke) showcased his research on this topic at the SASI 4 workshop co-located with ECSA 2020. Using two central use cases, he presents the minimum set of data that needs to be contained in Digital Twins to enable service-based production. For more information concerning the SASI 4 workshop, click here: http://events.disim.univaq.it/SASI4 Do you want to learn more about Digital Twins and the IT infrastructure needed for their support? Our Industry 4.0 experts Frank Schnicke and Thomas Kuhn provide an overview of the Industry 4.0 IT architecture of the future on the IESE blog: https://s.fhg.de/it40 Are you interested in instantiating the factory of the future? Contact us today!},
